\title{DoExp: Design of Experiments with Hasse Diagrams and Anatomy Tables}
\description{
Constructs Hasse diagrams and anatomy tables from structural formulas and experimental data sets. Hasse diagrams may display sources of variation and their degrees of freedom for general experimental structures. For orthogonal designs, the package can also compute core matrices associated with quadratic forms for sums of squares and contributions to the expected mean squares. Anatomy tables display the degrees of freedom and A-efficiencies associated with the sources of variation.
